This package provides a static C++ library for formatted text output.

The 'print' library offers simple functions to output text to various
streams (stdout, files, string streams) with formatting support.

Key features:
- Thread-safe output operations
- Support for custom delimiters and line endings
- Easy integration with existing C++ projects

Example usage:
    #include <print.hpp>
    print("Hello, World!", std::cout);

This package contains the development files (headers and static library)
required to build applications using the print library.

Dependencies: C++14 compatible compiler, CMake 3.10 or higher.

This library is distributed under the MIT license.
